WEBVTT

00:18.643 --> 00:20.311
Damn it. Seriously?

00:20.395 --> 00:21.563
CHOI TAE-HO

00:34.325 --> 00:38.204
MR. OH, HWANG YANG-JUNG
LEE DU-YEONG, HYEON-JU

00:46.755 --> 00:49.674
- Aren't you going home?
- I was just house-hunting, sir.

00:51.134 --> 00:53.720
Man, it's not easy
buying a house nowadays.

00:54.429 --> 00:55.263
Taking a honeymoon?

00:56.431 --> 01:00.101
My wife wants us to go to Paris,
but I don't think we'll go with COVID.

01:00.185 --> 01:01.978
Ugh, goddamn COVID.

01:06.191 --> 01:07.901
How come you're here so late, sir?

01:12.072 --> 01:14.824
So, something big came in.

01:15.867 --> 01:19.204
I've been keeping tabs on a loan shark
for about half a year now,

01:19.287 --> 01:21.664
and this fucking asshole
takes videos of people,

01:21.748 --> 01:23.583
so he has something to threaten them with.

01:24.417 --> 01:27.796
And today I happened to receive
a list of all the asshole's victims.

01:28.338 --> 01:29.422
I'll share it with you.

01:29.506 --> 01:32.092
I'll organize the data,
and we can dive into it together.

01:33.927 --> 01:35.303
Sounds good, sir.

01:36.721 --> 01:37.972
- Get back to searching.
- Will do.

01:43.186 --> 01:44.020
Mm.

01:44.104 --> 01:45.688
He said he got the list today.

01:46.981 --> 01:48.650
He probably didn't do it alone.

01:49.359 --> 01:52.654
Find me the asshole who helped him,
and I'll pay you 100 million per person.

01:53.822 --> 01:54.989
Yes, sir.

01:55.573 --> 01:57.700
When will you get Oh In-muk's location?

01:57.784 --> 02:00.203
I think I can find
his credit card locations

02:00.286 --> 02:04.582
of the last seven days…
probably by tomorrow morning.

02:06.167 --> 02:08.545
I'll pay you as soon as I receive it.
Good luck.

02:14.175 --> 02:15.385
A hundred million.

02:17.637 --> 02:18.680
What's up?,

02:20.431 --> 02:23.518
The only person who knew
where hard drive was, was Jang-do.

02:23.601 --> 02:26.688
The asshole must have snitched
when President Choi nabbed him.

02:27.814 --> 02:32.902
The fuckers who were with him
teamed up with Hong. Fucking shithead.

02:33.486 --> 02:34.362
Oppa.

02:35.321 --> 02:38.825
You said there's only one hard drive?

02:40.451 --> 02:42.245
There's only one hard drive.

02:44.080 --> 02:47.250
But everything's backed up on a laptop

02:47.333 --> 02:50.170
that we use to transfer the videos
to the drive.

02:52.547 --> 02:53.631
Oh!

02:55.216 --> 02:57.260
For now, we should just stay put.

02:58.761 --> 03:00.889
If we release that video
at the wrong time,

03:01.389 --> 03:06.436
then that son of a bitch, Hong,
is going to hit us with a tax audit.

03:06.519 --> 03:07.854
Stupid motherfucker.

03:10.940 --> 03:11.774
Oppa,

03:12.817 --> 03:16.279
wouldn't it be better to let them know
you still have the video?

03:19.157 --> 03:20.533
You need to scare them.

03:26.331 --> 03:28.541
You're a smart cookie, aren't you?

03:29.375 --> 03:30.585
A toast!

03:31.085 --> 03:32.295
- And cheers!
- Cheers!

03:36.799 --> 03:39.093
ADDRESS, MART
GAS STATION, RICE STORE

03:55.944 --> 03:58.738
GOHEUNG GROCERIES

03:59.447 --> 04:00.823
Have you seen this person before?

04:00.907 --> 04:02.325
Uh, I'm not sure.

04:02.408 --> 04:05.328
Our customers walk around in masks,
so it's hard to tell.

04:06.287 --> 04:07.705
Oh, yeah? Is that so?

04:08.206 --> 04:09.415
Ah, fuck me.

04:10.667 --> 04:11.834
Right, take another look.

04:15.588 --> 04:16.839
Oh.

04:17.340 --> 04:18.383
I really don't know.

04:18.466 --> 04:19.717
You think this is funny?

04:20.260 --> 04:22.762
- Excuse me?
- Do you think this is fucking funny?

04:22.845 --> 04:24.264
Uh, no, that's not what I--

04:25.682 --> 04:26.891
Goddammit.

04:27.725 --> 04:28.810
Eyes down, shithead.

04:29.560 --> 04:31.604
Look. Do you know him?

04:31.688 --> 04:32.730
I… I don't know.

04:32.814 --> 04:36.067
Yes or no, you little fuck!
Get up, get up, get up!

04:36.150 --> 04:37.568
- Do you know him or not?
- I don't know him.

04:37.652 --> 04:40.321
Do you know him or not, you piece of shit?
I said look at him. Look.

04:40.863 --> 04:42.240
Speak up, you fucking shit.

04:42.907 --> 04:44.200
Ah, fuck this.

04:44.701 --> 04:45.535
Look at the picture.

04:45.618 --> 04:47.870
- Hello, sir.
- Oh, hello. Welcome.

04:47.954 --> 04:49.622
- I'd like to ask you something.
- Okay, okay.

04:49.706 --> 04:53.293
I'm looking for someone.
He's a friend of my dad's.

04:54.919 --> 04:56.546
Oh, yes, I know him.

04:56.629 --> 04:58.631
- You know this man?
- I do, but what's this about?

04:58.715 --> 04:59.924
Well, I'm getting married,

05:00.008 --> 05:01.968
and I'd like to send him
a wedding invitation.

05:02.051 --> 05:03.052
Oh.

05:03.136 --> 05:04.262
Do you know where he lives?

05:04.345 --> 05:07.682
Of course. After all,
I deliver rice there every month.

05:08.433 --> 05:10.727
Could I get an address from you?

05:11.227 --> 05:12.437
Oh, sure. I'll get it for you.

05:51.642 --> 05:54.854
BLOODHOUNDS

06:01.027 --> 06:01.861
He's here.

06:05.948 --> 06:07.492
Kang In-beom's profile.

06:08.117 --> 06:10.661
His info right, right, right here, guys.

06:11.412 --> 06:12.288
Ah.

06:12.372 --> 06:13.748
You work fast.

06:14.248 --> 06:16.417
Every second counts
in situations like this.

06:16.501 --> 06:18.419
- Thank you very much.
- All right.

06:19.379 --> 06:20.213
- It's done.
- Yeah.

06:37.397 --> 06:39.190
This is it?

06:39.273 --> 06:40.149
Huh?

06:41.192 --> 06:43.069
Ah, so you don't know?

06:43.986 --> 06:47.573
Normally, when you make
someone do something like this,

06:48.533 --> 06:52.412
- You give a little token of thanks.
- Oh, right. How much should we give you?

06:53.454 --> 06:54.747
You know, a one piece.

06:54.831 --> 07:00.628
I mean, we're… we're a team and family.
A big one will do. Yeah!

07:00.711 --> 07:01.879
- Okay, all right.
- Yeah.

07:01.963 --> 07:03.256
Thank you.

07:04.757 --> 07:06.342
Hey, call me whenever you need something.

07:06.426 --> 07:08.386
- Will do. Have a nice day.
- Good night, then.

07:08.469 --> 07:09.303
Mm.

07:20.440 --> 07:22.108
Fuck, man. I meant a million won.

07:25.319 --> 07:27.530
PERSONAL INFORMATION
KANG IN-BEOM

07:34.579 --> 07:36.747
She told us not to use it though.

07:37.457 --> 07:40.209
We have to look at it on a big screen
to get a better look at his neighborhood.

07:40.293 --> 07:42.462
Right. What if Da-min comes in
while we're at it.

07:43.337 --> 07:46.257
She won't. We got caught before
because she was passing by.

07:46.340 --> 07:47.592
It was bad luck.

07:49.760 --> 07:52.638
- "Gangdong-gu, Seonggu-ro."
- "Seonggu-ro."

07:57.935 --> 08:00.188
I told you she'd come.
Turn it off.

08:00.271 --> 08:01.230
Oh, God.

08:06.986 --> 08:08.279
Uh, what are you doing?

08:09.405 --> 08:11.866
It smells like lonely men in here.

08:12.742 --> 08:14.327
Why are you using the computer again?

08:14.410 --> 08:15.786
I told you not to.

08:16.579 --> 08:17.497
We're sorry.

08:17.580 --> 08:19.624
Also, sorry about the lonely man smell.

08:19.707 --> 08:20.958
Damn.

08:21.042 --> 08:23.377
Whatever. This room is ruined.

08:23.461 --> 08:24.295
It's ruined.

08:24.378 --> 08:25.254
Da-min!

08:26.714 --> 08:29.008
- What is it?
- I'm also sorry about today.

08:29.091 --> 08:30.676
I'll take care of this putrid smell.

08:31.302 --> 08:32.386
How will you?

08:32.470 --> 08:33.387
A diffuser.

08:33.888 --> 08:37.683
A diffuser will get rid of
this sad old-man smell.

08:37.767 --> 08:38.601
Really?

08:38.684 --> 08:40.770
First of all, to get rid of a bad smell,

08:40.853 --> 08:42.563
you just have to find
an opposing good scent.

08:42.647 --> 08:45.733
This sad old-man smell is
basically a blend of a thick, musky odor

08:45.816 --> 08:47.818
with slight, unintentional undertones
of rotten wood.

08:47.902 --> 08:49.820
To get rid of it,
we need the opposing scent.

08:50.988 --> 08:53.950
Something floral and fruity.

08:54.033 --> 08:55.952
I use Baies, Baies from Diptyque.

08:56.035 --> 08:57.870
- I like that one.
- Well, all right.

08:58.579 --> 08:59.580
Then we're in luck!

08:59.664 --> 09:02.250
The fresh sweetness in the Baies
will cancel out

09:02.333 --> 09:05.461
all the sad old-man smell here.

09:06.629 --> 09:08.589
We'll get you one
when we leave this place.

09:09.215 --> 09:10.633
- A gift.
- Yeah.

09:10.716 --> 09:12.677
We'll get you one for the ground floor,
one for the top bunk.

09:12.760 --> 09:13.803
Bathroom too.

09:13.886 --> 09:15.346
Okay, three it is.

09:15.429 --> 09:16.305
Deal.

09:26.482 --> 09:28.818
Dude, how does Kang In-beom
know my number? He's calling now.

09:30.027 --> 09:31.153
Whoa, no way.

09:31.237 --> 09:32.780
Something must be wrong here, right?

09:41.205 --> 09:42.206
Oh god.

09:43.332 --> 09:45.042
What's wrong with Grandpa?

09:46.085 --> 09:47.253
Who did this to him?

09:47.753 --> 09:48.588
Uh…

09:52.300 --> 09:53.175
No!

09:53.676 --> 09:56.387
Come to Incheon's
Four Garden shopping mall in one hour.

09:57.096 --> 10:00.224
Call the cops, and the old man dies.

10:00.308 --> 10:01.517
You're fucking dead.

10:03.311 --> 10:04.228
Uh…

10:04.312 --> 10:06.314
Uh, Da-min, you should tell us
what he said too.

10:06.981 --> 10:08.858
He said to come to Four Garden mall
in an hour.

10:08.941 --> 10:10.693
He said if we call the cops,

10:12.278 --> 10:13.279
he'll kill Grandpa.

10:16.032 --> 10:17.950
Come on.
There's not much time.

10:33.215 --> 10:34.467
Gun-woo.

10:34.550 --> 10:37.219
- How many do you think will be there?
- Uh, at least 30.

10:37.303 --> 10:38.471
They'll probably have weapons.

10:38.554 --> 10:41.307
and, uh, Kang In-beom and Mr. Jung
will probably be there.

10:42.099 --> 10:44.226
Do you think it would be a good idea
to call Gang-yong?

10:44.894 --> 10:48.814
No, that would put Mr. Oh
in too much danger.

10:48.898 --> 10:52.360
- What about our senior?
- Which senior?

10:52.443 --> 10:53.277
You know, Mr. Moon.

10:54.570 --> 10:55.613
But he hurt his arm, right?

10:55.696 --> 10:57.657
Wouldn't he help in any way that he could?

10:57.740 --> 10:59.492
Uh, that's true, but…

11:00.993 --> 11:01.994
You two ready?

11:02.078 --> 11:05.414
Yes, but Da-min, what's the bow for?

11:06.123 --> 11:07.083
For rescuing Grandpa.

11:07.166 --> 11:09.794
Uh, no. There's no way.
We'll go just the two of us.

11:09.877 --> 11:11.253
It's too dangerous for you.

11:13.339 --> 11:14.423
Move over.

11:14.507 --> 11:16.926
Da-min, why would you--

11:17.009 --> 11:18.219
Whoa!

11:26.519 --> 11:27.812
I also know how to fight.

11:28.938 --> 11:30.690
I'm coming, so don't try to stop me.

11:32.274 --> 11:34.235
What are you doing? We don't have time.

11:34.860 --> 11:36.862
Hey, she's a good shot.

11:36.946 --> 11:37.780
Hey,

11:38.572 --> 11:39.907
I think she'll be useful.

11:43.994 --> 11:45.538
Hello, sir, it's Woo-jin.

11:46.831 --> 11:47.665
Mr. Oh…

11:49.458 --> 11:50.501
…has been kidnapped.

11:52.294 --> 11:54.296
Can you, uh, help us in any way?

11:54.380 --> 11:56.507
I'm also indebted to Mr. Oh.

11:57.508 --> 11:59.552
Don't go in without me, no matter what.

12:00.302 --> 12:01.262
That's an order.

12:48.350 --> 12:51.353
MOON GWANG-MU
734TH CLASS SENIOR

13:04.492 --> 13:06.243
My Junior Marines, you're finally here.

13:06.327 --> 13:08.829
- Yes, sir.
- Wow, sir, you've really gone all out.

13:08.913 --> 13:11.332
Oh, yeah, I had this lying around.

13:11.874 --> 13:14.210
It really itches. I think it's pretty old.

13:14.293 --> 13:15.961
Should probably take it off soon.

13:28.432 --> 13:30.684
Through the underground parking lot,
I'll--

13:30.768 --> 13:31.685
Wait, who are you?

13:32.269 --> 13:33.687
I'm here to rescue my grandpa.

13:35.356 --> 13:36.816
She's Mr. Oh's granddaughter.

13:37.650 --> 13:39.318
Oh. Oh, right.

13:39.401 --> 13:41.111
Your faces are similar. I can see it.

13:41.195 --> 13:42.822
It's almost been an hour.

13:43.405 --> 13:44.448
Right, right.

13:44.532 --> 13:45.741
And what's in the bag?

13:45.825 --> 13:47.117
It's a compound bow.

13:47.993 --> 13:48.828
A guobaorou?

13:49.453 --> 13:50.746
Compound bow.

13:50.830 --> 13:51.705
Guo--

13:51.789 --> 13:53.999
Sir, it's a competition bow.

13:54.083 --> 13:55.501
Uh-huh.

13:55.584 --> 13:58.045
Oh, right.
Koreans are really good at archery, yeah.

13:59.672 --> 14:00.673
Is she a good shot?

14:00.756 --> 14:01.882
She is.

14:03.300 --> 14:06.262
All right, so Archer and I will take
the stairs from the parking lot

14:06.345 --> 14:08.055
and make our way
to the top of the building.

14:08.138 --> 14:11.100
Our two Marines,
you charge in through the front gates.

14:11.183 --> 14:13.477
We'll cover fire from the top. Understood?

14:13.561 --> 14:14.854
- Yes, sir.
- Let's move.

14:15.938 --> 14:16.897
Go.

14:16.981 --> 14:17.982
- Follow me.
- Okay.

14:24.029 --> 14:25.531
- This way.
- Right, okay.

14:58.689 --> 14:59.899
Where is Mr. Oh?

15:01.317 --> 15:02.818
Kill them!

15:16.373 --> 15:18.876
One, two, three!

15:51.742 --> 15:52.743
Wow.

15:52.826 --> 15:53.953
- Good job.
- Get them.

15:54.036 --> 15:55.537
Where? Who is it?

15:58.165 --> 16:00.960
What is it?
Where is it coming from?

16:02.795 --> 16:04.296
Hey, hey!

16:04.380 --> 16:05.547
Up there!

16:05.631 --> 16:07.132
Get the black one. The black one.

16:07.216 --> 16:08.550
Who is it? Who's doing this?

16:17.601 --> 16:19.311
The blue one there. There, the guy there.

16:23.983 --> 16:24.817
Damn it.

16:24.900 --> 16:26.902
You keep helping out the juniors, okay?

16:27.403 --> 16:28.904
Oh, fuck. Fuck!

16:35.577 --> 16:36.495
Hey there, blue boy.

16:38.038 --> 16:39.540
Are you on the track team or something?

16:40.124 --> 16:41.291
Fucking shit!

17:04.398 --> 17:05.274
Get lost!

17:33.594 --> 17:35.596
What are you doing? Get up.

18:22.309 --> 18:23.352
Shit.

19:04.726 --> 19:05.561
Shit!

19:20.284 --> 19:22.578
Guess you need a knife to beat me,
huh, tough guy?

19:22.661 --> 19:24.955
Then pull it out, asshole.

19:26.123 --> 19:26.999
Come on.

19:32.296 --> 19:33.881
You've got pride, after all.

19:35.757 --> 19:36.592
Let's go.

20:18.592 --> 20:19.968
Oh, hey, are you…

20:20.052 --> 20:20.886
…are you all right?

20:20.969 --> 20:22.054
Not really.

21:00.968 --> 21:03.845
One, two, three, four!

21:03.929 --> 21:06.682
One, two, three, four!

21:29.621 --> 21:31.248
All right. Track guy.

21:31.832 --> 21:34.376
Hey! Hey, hey, hey, asshole. Wake up!

21:34.459 --> 21:36.128
Come on. Up, up, up!

21:36.211 --> 21:37.254
Up!

21:37.337 --> 21:38.672
So where's Mr. Oh?

21:40.257 --> 21:41.508
Look at this asshole.

21:41.591 --> 21:43.510
Does he think he's being a tough guy
or something?

21:43.593 --> 21:45.762
- Hey, Archer, give me an arrow quick!
- Huh?

21:46.346 --> 21:48.098
I'll give it back.
I just need it for a second.

21:48.181 --> 21:52.227
All right, let's see
what a loyal bloodhound this guy is.

21:52.728 --> 21:54.187
I was like you, you know?

21:54.271 --> 21:56.356
Well, back when Mr. Choi was alive.

21:56.982 --> 22:01.987
But do you know what becomes
of a bloodhound that's lost its master?!

22:02.529 --> 22:05.866
It becomes a filthy stray
that mauls everyone in sight.

22:05.949 --> 22:06.992
Oh!

22:11.913 --> 22:13.790
Oh, no. No!

22:14.624 --> 22:16.793
This isn't pain that you're feeling.
It's just shock.

22:16.877 --> 22:18.503
The real pain comes

22:19.838 --> 22:22.257
when I pull this bad boy out!

22:25.385 --> 22:29.348
Hey guys, could you…
please cover Archer's ears for a second?

22:34.811 --> 22:36.063
You married, shithead?

22:37.230 --> 22:42.694
Because the important thing
in the whole world is family.

22:42.778 --> 22:46.531
But without this, buddy,
you'll never be able to make one.

22:48.033 --> 22:50.160
So, work or family?

22:50.243 --> 22:52.162
You better choose wisely.

22:53.038 --> 22:56.208
I gotta admit, you choose work right now,

22:56.291 --> 22:58.001
that's gonna make you a real pro.

22:58.085 --> 23:01.505
But obviously, in that case,
I'm gonna have to puncture your balls.

23:02.172 --> 23:05.092
"Why?" you ask. Because I'm also a pro.

23:06.134 --> 23:07.177
All right.

23:08.512 --> 23:10.055
You got three.

23:10.138 --> 23:11.264
Three,

23:11.348 --> 23:12.307
two,

23:13.642 --> 23:15.060
one.

23:15.727 --> 23:19.398
- Wait!
- What? Why, why, why?

23:21.233 --> 23:22.150
I'll talk, yeah.

23:27.280 --> 23:28.365
Tuck down, asshole.

23:29.658 --> 23:30.700
Get inside, hurry!

23:32.035 --> 23:34.204
I said fuckin' tuck down.

23:38.500 --> 23:41.253
Uh, sir, we'll go
and save Mr. Oh right away.

23:41.336 --> 23:43.171
Can you hold on to Kang In-beom
in the meantime?

23:43.255 --> 23:45.257
What are you talking about?
I'm coming with you guys.

23:45.340 --> 23:46.758
We're gonna do it ourselves.

23:47.801 --> 23:49.636
Your arm's in bad shape, sir.

23:50.220 --> 23:52.097
Fuck me.

23:52.180 --> 23:55.684
Uh, sir, Kang In-beom knows
where Kim Myeong-gil's slush funds are,

23:56.393 --> 23:58.520
plus the location
of the safe containing those funds

23:58.603 --> 23:59.646
and Mr. Choi's gold.

24:00.355 --> 24:03.483
Please get all that information out of him
using your Marine tactics.

24:03.567 --> 24:04.651
We need you, sir. Please.

24:05.527 --> 24:06.403
All right.

24:06.945 --> 24:07.779
You got it.

24:09.489 --> 24:10.907
You just get him back, okay?

24:11.491 --> 24:12.409
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

24:13.034 --> 24:14.244
Let's go. Da-min.

24:23.003 --> 24:24.921
NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

24:29.968 --> 24:30.844
Here.

24:32.262 --> 24:34.181
What do you think?

24:34.848 --> 24:38.768
Sir, I've seen him this prick
standing next to the chief of staff.

24:39.978 --> 24:41.021
The chief of staff?

24:41.104 --> 24:43.899
Yes, sir. The hooked nose and those ears.
I'm positive.

24:45.233 --> 24:47.527
Why would a scummy loan shark bribe
the presidential office?

24:47.611 --> 24:48.820
I bet he sticks his nose everywhere.

24:49.404 --> 24:51.948
Or he could be a bigger player
than we actually realize.

24:55.035 --> 24:56.995
HEAVY DRINKER GUN-WOO

24:58.330 --> 24:59.164
What's up?

24:59.247 --> 25:01.374
Hey, man, sorry for calling you
at such a late hour,

25:01.458 --> 25:04.002
but we didn't know what to do
in this situation, so we had to reach out.

25:04.586 --> 25:07.255
- What?
- Kim Myeong-gil, he kidnapped Mr. Oh.

25:07.339 --> 25:09.299
So I'm heading to Seoryeong
with Woo-jin right now.

25:09.382 --> 25:10.550
Just the two of you?

25:10.634 --> 25:12.427
Why the hell
are you only telling me this now?

25:12.511 --> 25:13.345
I'm sorry,

25:13.428 --> 25:16.598
but they told us that they'd kill Mr. Oh
if we said anything to the cops.

25:16.681 --> 25:17.682
Hold on.

25:18.600 --> 25:20.393
Did Kim Myeong-gil call you himself?

25:20.477 --> 25:22.270
No, no. We managed to capture
one of his thugs.

25:22.354 --> 25:23.522
He's the one who told us.

25:23.605 --> 25:26.107
So, you don't know for sure
if Kim Myeong-gil will be there?

25:26.191 --> 25:27.025
No.

25:28.944 --> 25:30.779
Send me the location. I'll head over now.

25:30.862 --> 25:32.364
Don't go in. Just wait for me, okay?

25:32.447 --> 25:33.323
Okay.

25:34.699 --> 25:36.493
- Dude, text him the info.
- Okay.

25:40.997 --> 25:41.831
Sir.

25:41.915 --> 25:44.459
Jae-min,
come down to the meeting room right now.

25:45.210 --> 25:46.044
All right, sir.

25:54.094 --> 25:57.639
Hey, listen here. Call in some backup.
It's Buseong-myeon in Seoryeong.

25:57.722 --> 25:59.766
It's about that thing
I mentioned last time.

25:59.849 --> 26:01.601
- Yes, sir.
- Thank you.

26:01.685 --> 26:03.311
When did you see them?

26:04.437 --> 26:05.480
About a month ago.

26:06.481 --> 26:07.899
LIEUTENANT KIM JAE-MIN

26:10.402 --> 26:11.236
Mm.

26:22.789 --> 26:24.791
MR. KIM MYEONG-GIL

26:26.793 --> 26:28.753
The cops are on their way.

26:28.837 --> 26:29.879
Okay, got it.

26:38.138 --> 26:40.765
Yo, the cops are comin'. Clean up!

27:03.330 --> 27:05.332
All right.
Check if there's a back entrance.

27:05.415 --> 27:07.626
- Come on, quick. Quick, move out.
- Hurry up.

27:19.387 --> 27:20.513
Turn off the engine.

27:20.597 --> 27:21.431
Sorry.

27:21.973 --> 27:24.434
Hey, we'll see what's going on inside.
Wait here.

27:26.936 --> 27:30.106
We just searched the place.
There's nothing here but a flatfish farm.

27:30.690 --> 27:31.650
Oh…

27:33.526 --> 27:34.903
Maybe this guy will know something.

27:39.115 --> 27:40.408
Who the hell is this asshole?

27:40.909 --> 27:42.035
Kim Myeong-gil's thug.

27:42.744 --> 27:44.079
The one who stabbed me.

27:47.957 --> 27:50.377
I'm a cop, and I've got some questions
you need to answer.

27:52.629 --> 27:53.755
You prick, nod your head.

27:55.298 --> 27:56.716
Is Seoul Fish Farm the right place?

27:59.260 --> 28:00.720
Did anyone know that we were coming?

28:05.016 --> 28:06.017
Gang-yong.

28:06.643 --> 28:09.062
This guy's crew gave us the slip
in the middle of the fight.

28:09.729 --> 28:11.606
They might've given them a heads-up
before we got here.

28:16.444 --> 28:18.822
Let this guy out and leave now.

28:18.905 --> 28:20.365
You guys weren't here. Is that clear?

28:20.448 --> 28:21.491
- Okay.
- Okay.

28:21.574 --> 28:23.034
- Are you hurt?
- No.

28:24.035 --> 28:24.869
Han-gu.

28:35.213 --> 28:36.715
Where is Grandpa?

28:38.133 --> 28:39.300
We need to wait a little more.

28:39.384 --> 28:40.885
The detectives should get back to us.

28:41.469 --> 28:43.471
We don't have much time.

28:47.392 --> 28:48.435
We have to find him.

28:50.103 --> 28:51.438
No matter what it takes.

28:52.772 --> 28:54.482
The safe! Where's the safe?

28:55.108 --> 28:57.736
Come on, you fuckhead.
Where's Kim Myeong-gil's safe?

28:57.819 --> 28:59.195
Damn it! Come on!

28:59.279 --> 29:03.074
Listen, asshole, if you keep this up,
you're gonna end up dead, you hear me?

29:17.213 --> 29:18.631
Okay, give me a cigarette.

29:20.508 --> 29:21.593
You piece of shit!

29:26.347 --> 29:28.224
- Hit me!
- Fuck him!

29:28.308 --> 29:30.477
Hit me harder!

29:34.564 --> 29:37.108
BEST PORK
BEOMSEUNG DISTRIBUTION

29:46.868 --> 29:47.786
How'd it go?

29:48.411 --> 29:49.746
Why isn't Mr. Oh with you?

29:49.829 --> 29:50.997
Uh, we couldn't find him.

29:51.080 --> 29:53.249
I think his thugs caught on to us
and took him somewhere else.

29:53.333 --> 29:54.709
Damn it.

29:54.793 --> 29:55.835
That gym rat say anything?

29:55.919 --> 29:57.796
That's one stubborn fucker in there.

29:57.879 --> 29:59.130
He won't say a word.

30:04.385 --> 30:06.095
Having fun, huh?

30:08.097 --> 30:11.309
- You want fun? I'll show you fun.
- What the hell are you gonna do now?

30:23.613 --> 30:24.614
Shit!

30:25.198 --> 30:27.617
Sir! That idiot, he bit his tongue.

30:28.409 --> 30:29.869
- Fuck!
- Come on, sir!

30:31.538 --> 30:33.373
Goddammit! Fuck!

30:33.456 --> 30:35.583
- Hey! Hey!
- Fuck.

30:35.667 --> 30:37.794
- Hey, Kang In-beom, snap out of it! Hey!
- Damn it!

30:37.877 --> 30:40.797
- Dude, call an ambulance now.
- Okay.

30:41.297 --> 30:42.382
Uh, wait! Wait, wait!

30:42.966 --> 30:45.635
If we just send him off,
how will we find Kim Myeong-gil's safe?

30:45.718 --> 30:48.263
Still, we can't just stand here
and let a person die, sir.

30:49.055 --> 30:51.516
If he dies like this,
we still won't be able to get to the safe.

30:52.600 --> 30:53.935
Okay, give it to me quick.

30:54.477 --> 30:56.062
- You gotta let me get him down.
- Fuck!

30:56.145 --> 30:57.021
Okay. Come on.

31:03.903 --> 31:05.446
Sir! Sir, are you all right?

31:06.281 --> 31:08.366
Sir, wake up! Are you okay?

31:14.747 --> 31:15.915
Hello.

31:15.999 --> 31:18.751
- Hello.
- Where's the owner?

31:19.252 --> 31:20.712
Oh, yes, she went on vacation.

31:21.296 --> 31:22.130
Oh.

31:22.797 --> 31:25.008
I'd like an iced hand-drip coffee
with Ethiopian beans.

31:25.091 --> 31:25.925
All right.

31:27.427 --> 31:29.971
- Here you go. It'll be right out.
- All right. Thank you.

31:31.639 --> 31:32.932
MY HAPPY FAMILY, I'LL KEEP YOU SAFE

31:48.865 --> 31:51.492
CEO KIM MYEONG-GIL
ATTACHED FILE: 1 VIDEO FILE

31:57.123 --> 31:58.291
Oh shit!

32:04.380 --> 32:05.381
Hey, Min-beom.

32:06.257 --> 32:08.593
Kim Myeong-gil still has the video of me.

32:09.677 --> 32:10.803
He just sent it to me.

32:11.304 --> 32:12.138
Uh, but how?

32:15.934 --> 32:17.018
Hello?

32:17.101 --> 32:18.269
Gang-yong?

32:19.062 --> 32:20.271
Hello?

32:26.319 --> 32:27.153
Damn it!

32:33.868 --> 32:34.744
Fuck.

33:14.283 --> 33:15.493
Motherfucker.

33:20.707 --> 33:21.541
Salt.

33:21.624 --> 33:22.625
What?

33:22.709 --> 33:24.127
Salt!

33:48.860 --> 33:50.653
Someone's been hit by a car!

33:51.362 --> 33:52.238
What happened?

33:52.321 --> 33:54.741
Oh my God! I think someone died.

33:57.535 --> 33:59.287
MR. OH

34:02.206 --> 34:04.417
Gun-woo, hurry. Look.

34:13.009 --> 34:14.510
Hey, shitheads.

34:15.094 --> 34:17.013
Why make a big problem out of nothing?

34:18.848 --> 34:19.849
What do you want from us?

34:22.268 --> 34:24.562
Come to the fish farm today at 9:00 p.m.

34:25.146 --> 34:27.023
If you decide to call the cops again,

34:27.523 --> 34:30.026
I'll grind up the old man
and feed him to the fish.

34:30.735 --> 34:31.944
You got it?

34:33.071 --> 34:36.032
I've gotten rid of Min Gang-yong
and all his cronies,

34:36.115 --> 34:37.617
so there's no one else to help you.

34:38.117 --> 34:39.494
Oh, and one more thing,

34:40.078 --> 34:41.704
if you mess around, your mom's next.

34:41.788 --> 34:43.790
See you there.

34:47.418 --> 34:48.920
GANG-YONG

34:55.051 --> 34:56.969
How'd he get to Gang-yong? He's a cop.

34:57.804 --> 34:59.639
Dude, I think things
might get really dangerous.

34:59.722 --> 35:01.182
We should really go alone this time.

35:01.849 --> 35:02.809
Excuse me?

35:05.520 --> 35:06.646
How long have you been there?

35:06.729 --> 35:08.147
The whole time.

35:09.774 --> 35:12.610
Don't even try to leave me out.
I'm going to rescue Grandpa.

35:18.741 --> 35:19.575
Come with me.

35:29.752 --> 35:30.878
Listen, Woo-jin,

35:30.962 --> 35:34.090
if something bad were to happen
to Mr. Oh right in front of us,

35:34.924 --> 35:37.927
Da-min's definitely going to
break down like Hyeon-ju did and I…

35:39.262 --> 35:41.889
I never want to see
something like that happen again.

35:42.640 --> 35:43.516
But Gun-woo,

35:44.892 --> 35:46.644
one thing that's different from back then.

35:47.270 --> 35:48.396
You know what that is?

35:49.397 --> 35:50.273
Back then,

35:51.232 --> 35:53.734
the invincible Marine duo were apart.

35:54.652 --> 35:56.070
That's not the case now.

35:56.154 --> 35:59.073
And we're stronger. A lot strong.
You remember, right?

36:00.032 --> 36:01.909
One, two, three, four, five.

36:01.993 --> 36:03.703
One, two, three, four, five!

36:07.832 --> 36:08.708
Look,

36:10.376 --> 36:12.628
let's work together,
so we can save everyone.

36:13.671 --> 36:15.173
Mr. Oh, Da-min,

36:15.882 --> 36:18.467
the people that Kim Myeong-gil hurt.

36:23.472 --> 36:24.390
Ack?

36:24.473 --> 36:25.558
Ack!

36:27.268 --> 36:28.102
Ack!

36:29.187 --> 36:30.354
Ack!

36:41.115 --> 36:42.200
Why'd we stop?

36:42.909 --> 36:44.452
Woo-jin and I are gonna head in first.

36:44.535 --> 36:46.537
Keep a look
until you find a good spot to shoot from.

36:46.621 --> 36:47.580
That's when you move in.

36:47.663 --> 36:48.623
Sounds good.

36:49.498 --> 36:50.499
You should get out.

37:14.065 --> 37:16.400
They could've dropped me off closer.

37:20.279 --> 37:21.864
- Good thinking.
- Hm?

37:23.074 --> 37:26.077
Dropping Da-min off far away
so that she doesn't get hurt.

37:26.786 --> 37:29.956
Uh, I just didn't want her
to end up getting caught.

37:31.749 --> 37:32.750
Was it too far?

37:34.835 --> 37:36.379
It'll take her ten minutes.

37:36.462 --> 37:38.256
Then let's get this over with fast.

37:38.839 --> 37:39.674
Okay.

38:47.158 --> 38:48.909
Kill them!

38:52.663 --> 38:53.664
Get 'em.

38:53.748 --> 38:55.249
These guys have a shit ton of weapons.

39:02.882 --> 39:03.716
Dude!

39:45.508 --> 39:46.342
Son of a bitch!

40:20.459 --> 40:22.420
I'm gonna fuck you up, man!

40:22.503 --> 40:23.421
Oh shit.

40:28.217 --> 40:29.135
Hey.

40:30.177 --> 40:32.221
You can't even get rid of two kids?

40:34.432 --> 40:35.349
I'm sorry, sir.

40:35.433 --> 40:37.268
Sorry isn't fucking good enough.

40:41.355 --> 40:42.606
Now then.

40:44.024 --> 40:45.693
Come on!

40:47.111 --> 40:47.945
Now,

40:48.654 --> 40:52.366
you punks come any closer,
and I'll slit the old timer's throat.

40:52.450 --> 40:53.409
You understand me?

40:54.118 --> 40:56.328
Too bad. I wanted to do it.

41:04.462 --> 41:07.798
Hurry up and kill them, you stupid fucks!
What are you waiting for?

41:08.591 --> 41:10.301
Do I have to kill them? Huh?

41:10.384 --> 41:12.720
You sons of bitches are just unbelievable.

41:18.142 --> 41:19.143
Hey, duck!

41:27.776 --> 41:29.695
You fuckin' son of a bitch!

41:29.778 --> 41:32.156
Come here, you fucker! Come here!

41:32.239 --> 41:34.158
I told you to hurry up
and kill them, you assholes!

41:34.241 --> 41:36.035
What are you doing? Let go, motherfucker!

41:43.792 --> 41:45.586
I said let go of me!

41:48.172 --> 41:49.924
Kill them! Come on!

42:14.365 --> 42:15.282
Grandpa!

42:15.366 --> 42:17.076
Grandpa, are you okay?

42:17.159 --> 42:19.620
It's me, Da-min.

42:24.083 --> 42:24.959
Oh.

42:26.752 --> 42:29.213
You pulled out my eyebrows.

42:32.091 --> 42:33.300
Mr. Oh, are you all right?

42:35.761 --> 42:36.929
Thank you.

42:46.647 --> 42:48.357
Hurry up.

42:49.483 --> 42:52.111
- What's this?
- All right. All right, come on.

42:52.194 --> 42:54.113
Come on, get on it.
Hurry up and untie them.

43:01.495 --> 43:02.413
Who is it?

43:03.080 --> 43:04.206
Delivery.

43:13.382 --> 43:15.092
Ah, what the fuck.

43:15.926 --> 43:17.928
Stay still, you fucking asshole!

43:20.806 --> 43:22.641
Do a full sweep,
including the interior!

43:23.142 --> 43:24.935
- Scour every inch!
- What is this place?

43:28.063 --> 43:29.732
I found it! Everyone over here!

43:29.815 --> 43:30.983
Oh, God.

43:31.525 --> 43:34.695
What the hell? These guys are psychopaths.
What were they doing here?

43:38.866 --> 43:41.285
Ma'am, we from
the Serious Crime Investigation Division.

43:41.368 --> 43:43.287
I have a search warrant.

43:43.787 --> 43:46.457
As of right now, your property
will be subjected to search and seizure

43:46.540 --> 43:47.875
We'd appreciate your cooperation.

43:47.958 --> 43:48.792
Let's go.

43:49.460 --> 43:50.586
Come on. Hurry up.

43:55.883 --> 43:56.967
Mr. Kim Jae-min?

43:57.801 --> 44:00.095
You're under arrest
for murder, bribery, kidnapping.

44:01.305 --> 44:03.974
Fuck me. This is so fucked up, man.

44:04.642 --> 44:05.476
Let's go.

44:07.269 --> 44:09.480
- Sir, check it out.
- Wow.

44:18.656 --> 44:19.490
NATIONAL POLICE HOSPITAL

44:19.573 --> 44:22.117
Luckily we got the warrant quickly
and went into Kim Myeong-gil's house.

44:22.201 --> 44:24.370
A bunch of cell phones were found
in his closet.

44:25.037 --> 44:26.747
We traced the numbers.

44:26.830 --> 44:28.874
And they all belonged
to dead or missing individuals.

44:28.957 --> 44:31.168
This crazy asshole.

44:32.002 --> 44:34.463
He was storing the phones
that belonged to the people he killed.

44:35.214 --> 44:36.590
He can't escape this.

44:36.674 --> 44:38.717
Not even the American president
can help him.

44:38.801 --> 44:40.135
Could go overseas.

44:40.636 --> 44:42.971
He's a wanted man now. It won't be easy.

44:43.055 --> 44:46.183
Criminals frequently go to China
on cargo ships, don't they?

44:46.266 --> 44:48.435
Kim Myeong-gil is
a grade-A wanted criminal.

44:48.519 --> 44:50.729
We'll be focusing surveillance
on potential stowaway routes.

44:50.813 --> 44:52.606
He won't get out of Korea that easily.

44:52.690 --> 44:54.608
But it's not completely off the table.

44:56.151 --> 44:59.571
You all seem to think this is all over,
but I'm really on edge right now.

44:59.655 --> 45:01.615
That bastard still has that video of me.

45:01.699 --> 45:03.951
If he releases it at any time,
it's all over for me.

45:09.373 --> 45:10.290
Brother.

45:11.041 --> 45:13.627
I really have to see
that maniac behind bars.

45:14.253 --> 45:15.629
Min-beom.

45:18.590 --> 45:19.758
I understand.

45:23.220 --> 45:25.055
But just look at Han-gu's condition.

45:26.181 --> 45:27.850
And Tae-yeong is still in a coma.

45:28.976 --> 45:30.144
We just need some time.

45:38.402 --> 45:39.445
We're gonna help find him.

45:40.779 --> 45:42.698
It's not over till it's over for real.

45:43.866 --> 45:47.327
Um, is there any way you could find out
where Im Jang-do might be?

45:47.911 --> 45:48.954
Why do you need Im Jang-do?

45:49.037 --> 45:53.000
Im Jang-do's probably in hiding somewhere
trying to stay away from Kim Myeong-gil.

45:53.083 --> 45:57.504
I think maybe Im Jang-do may know
where Kim Myeong-gil might run off to.

45:57.588 --> 45:59.798
That's right.
Im Jang-do may have given him tips

45:59.882 --> 46:01.592
on how to smuggle himself
out of the country.

46:01.675 --> 46:03.927
He mentioned earlier
he was in charge of stuff like that.

46:04.845 --> 46:06.680
All right, I'll look into it.

46:14.104 --> 46:17.483
- All right, how much in cash?
- I think I can give you 18 million.

46:18.817 --> 46:22.029
Im Jang-do hasn't used
a phone or credit card under his name

46:22.112 --> 46:23.322
in the last six months.

46:24.406 --> 46:27.117
He's avoided anything
that might give us a lead.

46:27.201 --> 46:28.827
So we don't have anything?

46:29.411 --> 46:34.124
Well, so far all we've found
is his bank account number.

46:34.208 --> 46:37.961
And apparently, he did a cash withdrawal
last March in Suwon.

46:38.045 --> 46:39.546
Can't you follow that?

46:39.630 --> 46:43.091
We could, but we'll have to check
a few months' worth of security footage,

46:43.175 --> 46:45.344
which would take some time.

46:46.428 --> 46:48.806
Do you think
we could get his account number?

46:48.889 --> 46:49.807
IM JANG-DO
JOHAN BANK

46:49.890 --> 46:52.184
This prick is super strapped for cash,

46:52.267 --> 46:54.978
so wire some money into that account,
and when you send it,

46:55.062 --> 46:57.439
put down your phone number
under the sender's name.

46:57.523 --> 46:59.274
Then he'll contact you
straight away for sure.

46:59.358 --> 47:01.860
- How much should we send him?
- A big one should do.

47:02.444 --> 47:03.320
Ten thousand won?

47:04.404 --> 47:06.990
I was wondering
if I should mention this last time,

47:07.074 --> 47:09.952
but in this line of work,
"a big one" differs by the situation.

47:10.452 --> 47:12.579
That big one
from when I got you Kang In-beom's info,

47:12.663 --> 47:14.790
that was supposed to be a million won.

47:14.873 --> 47:15.999
A million won?

47:16.083 --> 47:19.169
It's cool. It's cool.
I'm not asking for that money now, okay?

47:19.253 --> 47:20.671
I'm not some greedy asshole.

47:20.754 --> 47:22.005
We're family, after all.

47:22.089 --> 47:24.633
Okay, in this case,
how much are we talking about?

47:24.716 --> 47:26.510
He'll laugh at a million won.

47:27.052 --> 47:27.886
Ten million.

47:29.471 --> 47:30.848
He'll bite right away.

47:40.274 --> 47:43.777
Your wounds aren't healing
because you keep drinking alcohol--

47:55.914 --> 47:57.624
- Doctor.
- Yes, sir.

47:58.208 --> 48:00.460
- Do your job.
- Yes, sir.

48:06.049 --> 48:07.050
Shit.

48:07.134 --> 48:08.302
Sixty-six,

48:08.927 --> 48:10.137
sixty-seven,

48:10.220 --> 48:12.222
sixty-eight, sixty-nine.

48:12.306 --> 48:13.765
Dude, someone's calling.

48:14.850 --> 48:16.018
There's no number.

48:22.274 --> 48:23.317
Hello?

48:28.155 --> 48:28.989
Hello?

48:32.409 --> 48:33.243
Hello?

48:35.078 --> 48:35.913
You.

48:36.747 --> 48:38.582
The kid that was with Mr. Choi, right?

48:42.210 --> 48:43.045
Yes.

48:43.962 --> 48:45.964
And the cops told you my account number.

48:47.841 --> 48:48.675
Why?

48:49.509 --> 48:50.761
Why did you send the money?

48:51.762 --> 48:53.430
Because Kim Myeong-gil is running away.

48:54.222 --> 48:55.098
Why?

48:55.682 --> 48:57.267
Police have raided his house

48:57.351 --> 48:59.895
and found substantial evidence
that he killed several people.

48:59.978 --> 49:02.272
- When was that?
- Two days ago.

49:03.273 --> 49:06.026
You know where
Kim Myeong-gil will run to, don't you?

49:08.862 --> 49:09.696
I do.

49:10.364 --> 49:11.531
Listen.

49:11.615 --> 49:14.743
We have to catch him.
Please help us find out where he is.

49:18.080 --> 49:19.289
How much will you pay?

49:22.125 --> 49:23.377
Uh, a big one.

49:23.460 --> 49:26.463
You've got to be fucking kidding me.

49:28.340 --> 49:30.217
- I want a billion.
- A billion?

49:30.300 --> 49:32.844
I trusted President Choi
and got royally fucked over.

49:32.928 --> 49:34.554
I deserve at least a billion.

49:34.638 --> 49:36.223
Okay, but we don't have--

49:36.306 --> 49:38.308
Within a few days,
Kim Myeong-gil will flee overseas

49:38.392 --> 49:40.143
using the method I taught him.

49:41.812 --> 49:43.188
You know my account, right?

49:44.231 --> 49:45.148
Think it over.

49:48.276 --> 49:50.153
That it so fucked.

49:51.029 --> 49:52.406
How will we ever get a billion won?

49:53.657 --> 49:55.575
Should we ask Mr. Oh
if he could do anything?

49:55.659 --> 49:57.202
Mr. Oh doesn't have money.

49:57.786 --> 50:00.372
The money he gave us back then
was all he had left.

50:00.914 --> 50:01.748
Hold up.

50:07.754 --> 50:08.797
How much do we have in there?

50:11.925 --> 50:13.427
I think around 300 million.

50:13.510 --> 50:14.803
It's nowhere enough.

50:18.015 --> 50:20.017
Should we ask Min-beom
if we could borrow some money?

50:20.100 --> 50:22.436
Im Jang-do's the one
who took that video of Min-beom.

50:23.520 --> 50:25.814
You think he'll help us with this?

50:26.773 --> 50:27.607
I don't know.

50:28.358 --> 50:31.194
But I think Min-beom's the only one
who could help us in this situation.

50:32.195 --> 50:33.989
Let's try asking him just once, mm?

50:42.539 --> 50:43.915
Sir, here they are.

50:49.713 --> 50:51.506
Do you guys trust Im Jang-do?

50:53.675 --> 50:54.509
Uh,

50:55.677 --> 51:00.223
we do think that he can help us find…
everything that we've been looking for.

51:01.266 --> 51:03.602
What if he pockets the money
and goes overseas?

51:04.269 --> 51:05.353
Then what do we do?

51:25.457 --> 51:26.291
If he does that,

51:26.958 --> 51:30.837
if Im Jang-do breaks his promise and runs,
we'll chase him down and catch him.

51:31.463 --> 51:33.840
This much I can promise, sir.
You have my word.

51:48.980 --> 51:50.440
Keep that promise.

51:52.067 --> 51:53.485
- Great.
- Great.

51:56.321 --> 51:58.782
1,000,000,000 RECEIVED

52:11.962 --> 52:14.798
- Okay, looks good. Move along.
- Okay.

52:15.549 --> 52:16.383
You can go.

53:09.811 --> 53:11.980
UNKNOWN CALLER

53:14.566 --> 53:15.901
Write this down.

53:15.984 --> 53:17.652
The day after tomorrow at 1:00 a.m.,

53:17.736 --> 53:21.239
a cargo ship called the Nike
is going to depart for Ho Chi Minh City.

53:21.323 --> 53:24.784
Kim Myeong-gil gave political donations
to a high-ranking Vietnamese official.

53:25.368 --> 53:27.495
He's going to take off
with all of his slush funds.

53:28.246 --> 53:30.999
The container number is 9004230.

53:31.499 --> 53:34.211
There will be a cargo truck
with all of his slush funds hidden inside.

53:34.294 --> 53:36.588
Should we move in
when Kim Myeong-gil's getting on the ship?

53:36.671 --> 53:38.590
It won't be easy to find
because it's a big ship.

53:38.673 --> 53:39.507
How will we find it?

53:40.091 --> 53:41.885
You guys get on the ship with him.

53:44.638 --> 53:46.556
You mean we should get on the ship
and go to Vietnam?

53:46.640 --> 53:48.183
Well, that's up to you, right?

53:48.683 --> 53:50.477
- Bye.
- Wait, wait, wait.

53:50.560 --> 53:53.188
What should we do then
if we decide to board that ship?

53:53.939 --> 53:55.565
I'll text you a contact of mine.

53:55.649 --> 53:57.484
Tell him I sent you
and try to work out a deal.

53:57.567 --> 53:59.778
Also, he really likes cash.

54:06.284 --> 54:07.202
That's the text.

54:16.253 --> 54:19.172
I didn't know what you'd need,
so I brought a little bit of everything.

54:20.632 --> 54:21.466
Thank you, sir.

54:21.549 --> 54:22.801
You two take care.

54:23.677 --> 54:24.636
Yes, sir.

54:25.804 --> 54:26.763
Okay?

54:27.973 --> 54:28.848
Yes.

54:31.309 --> 54:32.143
Let's go up.

54:33.186 --> 54:34.104
You go on ahead.

54:34.896 --> 54:35.814
I need a minute.

54:38.900 --> 54:39.901
Okay.

54:45.699 --> 54:47.450
Thank you so much for your help.

54:48.451 --> 54:49.953
No, we should be thanking you.

54:59.337 --> 55:01.506
Da-min, see you soon.

55:03.216 --> 55:04.801
- See you.
- Up you go.

55:08.430 --> 55:09.306
Oh.

55:10.432 --> 55:12.058
You have my number?

55:13.018 --> 55:13.852
Mm.

55:20.775 --> 55:21.609
Let's go.

55:32.329 --> 55:34.539
- Hello.
- Hey, you're on your way there?

55:35.332 --> 55:36.499
Yes, we're on our way.

55:37.375 --> 55:39.127
Don't get hurt, okay?

55:39.627 --> 55:40.462
Okay.

55:40.545 --> 55:42.797
Me and Gang-yong
will take care of the rest.

55:43.673 --> 55:44.799
Drive safe.

55:44.883 --> 55:45.717
Yeah.

56:20.335 --> 56:21.628
Let's hurry along then.

56:21.711 --> 56:24.422
- Just a second.
- We'll be right back.

56:37.060 --> 56:37.894
Dude.

56:41.398 --> 56:42.232
Okay.

56:55.829 --> 56:56.663
Set sail.

57:07.549 --> 57:09.884
- Okay, go check out the inside first.
- Got it.

57:52.093 --> 57:53.178
Kim Myeong-gil!

58:24.626 --> 58:25.627
Uh-huh.

58:25.710 --> 58:26.544
Uh-huh.

58:34.552 --> 58:35.386
Oh!

01:02:57.482 --> 01:02:59.150
If you ever show your face again…

01:03:01.986 --> 01:03:03.070
I'll kill you.

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:49.325
Gun-woo.

01:03:53.746 --> 01:03:54.664
Are you all right?

01:04:06.884 --> 01:04:07.718
What is it?

01:04:10.930 --> 01:04:11.764
Dude.

01:04:15.685 --> 01:04:17.144
I've become a bloodhound.

01:04:35.079 --> 01:04:38.291
Gun-woo, have you forgotten
about the heart of a boxer?

01:04:39.917 --> 01:04:41.919
All we have to do is find our way back.

01:04:42.712 --> 01:04:43.546
Hm?

01:04:44.130 --> 01:04:45.464
Let's go back together.

01:04:51.178 --> 01:04:52.013
Mm-hm.

01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:53.931
Let's go back.

01:05:02.857 --> 01:05:03.691
Here.

01:05:22.585 --> 01:05:23.753
Whoa! Dude!

01:05:27.590 --> 01:05:30.384
Ah, yes!

01:05:38.809 --> 01:05:39.644
Hey.

01:05:39.727 --> 01:05:42.271
- Hey, man, where are you?
- I'm almost there.

01:05:42.980 --> 01:05:44.523
Gold bars, did you find them?

01:05:45.107 --> 01:05:46.692
Yes, we found them all.

01:05:47.860 --> 01:05:48.694
And the phone?

01:05:50.404 --> 01:05:51.530
I'll go get it.

01:05:51.614 --> 01:05:54.533
- Oh, dude, here. Here.
- Oh, oh, oh! Let's go!

01:05:54.617 --> 01:05:55.451
Right!

01:06:04.251 --> 01:06:05.294
How'd it go?

01:06:05.378 --> 01:06:07.254
I finally got the phone.

01:06:10.424 --> 01:06:11.300
They did good.

01:06:12.051 --> 01:06:14.971
I asked Interpol for backup.
They'll be waiting in Vietnam.

01:06:16.055 --> 01:06:17.223
It's all over.

01:06:17.306 --> 01:06:19.392
You really went through a lot, kiddo.

01:06:19.475 --> 01:06:20.434
Thank you.

01:06:36.367 --> 01:06:38.119
What would you guys like to do with this?

01:06:40.246 --> 01:06:41.205
Hm.

01:06:42.665 --> 01:06:46.794
Well, Mr. Choi always wanted to help
those who were too poor

01:06:46.877 --> 01:06:48.504
to get proper medical treatment,

01:06:49.797 --> 01:06:53.634
so I'd like this money to be spent
in accordance with Mr. Choi's wishes.

01:06:54.593 --> 01:06:55.928
What do you think about that idea?

01:06:57.430 --> 01:06:59.348
Don't you want the money for yourself?

01:07:03.144 --> 01:07:05.271
Uh, of course, I do.

01:07:06.105 --> 01:07:07.982
But this isn't my money.

01:07:08.983 --> 01:07:09.817
To be fair,

01:07:09.900 --> 01:07:12.236
I'm just trying to pay back Mr. Choi
for his kindness

01:07:12.319 --> 01:07:14.238
and make I sure I keep the promise
I made to him.

01:07:16.198 --> 01:07:17.199
Mm.

01:07:17.783 --> 01:07:19.076
Guys.

01:07:20.244 --> 01:07:23.247
We have a total of 168 golden bars,

01:07:23.330 --> 01:07:25.833
and each one would give us 500 million,

01:07:25.916 --> 01:07:27.877
putting us at 84 billion in total.

01:07:27.960 --> 01:07:30.463
If you want, I'll take this

01:07:30.546 --> 01:07:33.841
and start a welfare foundation
all under Iil Group.

01:07:33.924 --> 01:07:35.342
Through that welfare foundation,

01:07:35.426 --> 01:07:38.345
we'll be able to provide
medical assistance to people who need it.

01:07:39.305 --> 01:07:40.139
On top of that,

01:07:40.222 --> 01:07:42.349
I should just have our company
add some money to the pot,

01:07:43.100 --> 01:07:44.727
set up a hospital while we're at it.

01:07:45.269 --> 01:07:47.354
- Well, that sounds like a great idea.
- Right?

01:07:47.438 --> 01:07:48.439
It does.

01:07:48.522 --> 01:07:50.399
I think my dad will like it too.

01:07:51.025 --> 01:07:53.277
And it'll help
with our company image as well.

01:07:53.360 --> 01:07:55.237
Besides, we'll do the world a lot of good.

01:07:56.280 --> 01:07:58.491
I'll get started
as soon as I'm done with the hotel.

01:07:58.574 --> 01:07:59.408
One last thing.

01:08:00.701 --> 01:08:03.370
Could you maybe include Mr. Choi
in the hospital name?

01:08:03.996 --> 01:08:06.540
- What was his name?
- His full name was Choi Tae-ho.

01:08:07.083 --> 01:08:09.877
To be honest,
I don't think it'll be that easy,

01:08:10.795 --> 01:08:12.421
but I'll definitely consider it.

01:08:12.505 --> 01:08:13.672
Thank you so much.

01:08:21.305 --> 01:08:22.515
Huh?

01:08:22.598 --> 01:08:24.975
I'll cover the missing amount
with my own money.

01:08:25.059 --> 01:08:27.228
Think of it as a bonus
for a job well done.

01:08:27.728 --> 01:08:28.646
Um, it's all right.

01:08:28.729 --> 01:08:29.897
We're really good.

01:08:30.397 --> 01:08:32.483
That Mr. Choi would have done the same.

01:08:33.109 --> 01:08:33.943
Take it.

01:08:38.948 --> 01:08:41.325
What, you don't know
what to say all of a sudden?

01:08:44.286 --> 01:08:45.621
A thank you would do.

01:08:47.039 --> 01:08:49.250
- Thank you so much, Mr. Choi.
- No.

01:08:51.001 --> 01:08:52.878
I'm the one that should be thanking you.

01:08:56.257 --> 01:08:57.341
Thank you so much!

01:09:07.226 --> 01:09:10.020
Let's get the ball.
Come on. Stop her!

01:09:12.231 --> 01:09:14.650
There, right?

01:09:18.362 --> 01:09:19.196
Oh!

01:09:20.156 --> 01:09:21.365
Gun-woo, is that you?

01:09:22.241 --> 01:09:23.409
What? Where are you?

01:09:25.744 --> 01:09:27.413
Gun-woo!

01:09:27.913 --> 01:09:29.331
Oh! Oh!

01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:35.713
Oh!

01:09:40.926 --> 01:09:41.927
Oh, my son.

01:09:42.011 --> 01:09:43.512
Ah!

01:09:44.471 --> 01:09:46.557
Oh!

01:09:48.058 --> 01:09:49.018
Woo-jin.

01:09:49.894 --> 01:09:53.105
Oh my gosh, look at you.
What happened to your face?

01:09:53.689 --> 01:09:55.649
God, you went through so much.

01:09:59.528 --> 01:10:01.530
It's all over, Mom. Let's go home now.

01:10:02.072 --> 01:10:03.073
All right. Okay.

01:10:04.575 --> 01:10:06.744
Oh God, I'm so proud of you!

01:10:06.827 --> 01:10:08.787
Ah!
